# subordinate GID ranges for rootless containers (podman, buildah, crun)
#
# Format: user:start:count
#
# This file is shipped with comments only.  Do not remove it: shadow's
# useradd(8) assigns SUB_GID_COUNT (65536, from /etc/login.defs) to new
# accounts with UID >= 1000 only when /etc/subgid already exists.
#
# The Browneye installer adds the administrative user's range explicitly,
# for example for an account that already exists:
#   usermod --add-subgids 100000-165535 <user>
